WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.218
Where should we inspect?

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.614
The U B one thousand pair sits opposite each other at one height.

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:12.051
One transmits; the other receives.

00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:14.809
This scene shows the arrangement.

00:00:15.747 --> 00:00:18.220
The next view shows the simulated pulse.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.451
A simulated pulse crosses sound wood.

00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:28.459
Below, the trace shows the receiver response while the animation repeats.

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:31.733
Later waves reflect around the section.

00:00:32.671 --> 00:00:36.828
Acoustic parameters are illustrative; the colour scale stays the same.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.909
Decay changes this simulated response.

00:00:43.651 --> 00:00:46.572
Compare the section trace with the sound reference below.

00:00:47.509 --> 00:00:51.218
Reflection, scattering and damping can affect the waveform.

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:56.232
A large peak alone does not establish strength: overlapping waves can

00:00:56.246 --> 00:00:57.591
reinforce one another.

00:00:59.233 --> 00:01:01.434
This number is a timber bending estimate.

00:01:03.176 --> 00:01:07.972
It uses geometry, material inputs and defects in a separate structural

00:01:07.986 --> 00:01:08.421
model.

00:01:09.358 --> 00:01:12.334
The acoustic animation cannot measure fibre strength.

00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:17.674
Approved device calibration and interpretation remain separate requirements.
